  "description": "A governess in exile and the icy Duke of the North, a romance that blossoms at the end of a bitter winter. \n\nJeanne, the daughter of a fallen noble family, becomes a governess to make ends meet. She is exiled to the Duchy of the North for giving her student an enlightenment book. The ruler of that domain is Duke Baldr, who governs the bleak North while raising his late brother’s child alone. As he tests whether Jeanne is suitable to be his nephew’s governess, he finds his gaze repeatedly drawn to her upright and virtuous demeanor. A sprout of spring begins to bud in his heart, which had been frozen solid like the bitter winter. \n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
